title: Dashboard › Request drawer › Approve the write-back
route: /dashboard?request=R-0951
intro: After a payer approves, the approval number and dates go to the EMR only when a person confirms, and only while write-back is on in EMR Connect. The pop-up shows exactly three things. In the demo the EMR write is simulated and changes only the request's history.
dir: TD
also: Real world: writing the reference number, units and dates back to the EMR is a confirmed step. Demo only: the EMR write is simulated.
---
start s1 "Click 'Approve write-back' in the green box\nThe box shows only while write-back is on in EMR Connect"
overlay o1 "Pop-up 'Approve the write-back'\n'R-0951 · Evergreen'\n'EMR Connect will write only these three things to the chart. No notes, diagnoses or identifiers are written.'"
screen sc "Three facts\nApproval number 'PA-26-102944'\nApproved '14 days'\nDates '10/20 to 11/3'"
process p0 "Amount by program: Residential 3.5 14 days, PHP 10 days, Detox 5 days, IOP 24 units over 14 days"

click c1 "Click 'Write to the EMR'"
process p1 "Button shows a spinner for 1.1 seconds\n'Cancel' is disabled; the X, the dimmed area and Escape do nothing"
ext x1 "EMR receives the approval number and dates\n(demo: simulated)"
store w1 "What happens next becomes 'Next review booked. Written to the EMR'"
store w2 "History gets 'You confirmed the write-back'\nand 'Cadence wrote the approval number (PA-26-102944) and the dates to the EMR'"
toast t1 "'Written to the EMR'\n'PA-26-102944 and the approved dates are in the chart. Nothing else was written.'"
process p2 "Pop-up closes\nThe green box disappears because the next step no longer says Write-back"
end e1 "Request stays Approved, in Decided today"

click c2 "Click 'Cancel'"
click c3 "Click the X 'Close'"
click c4 "Click the dimmed area"
end e2 "Pop-up closes\nNothing is written; the green box stays"
click c5 "Press Escape"
process p3 "Escape closes only the pop-up\nThe drawer stays open; a second Escape closes it"
end e3 "Back in the drawer\nNothing is written; the green box stays"
process p4 "A write that has started always finishes and its toast appears\nEven if the drawer is closed in the meantime (browser Back)"

s1 --> o1 --> sc --> p0
sc --> c1 --> p1 --> x1 --> w1 --> w2 --> t1 --> p2 --> e1
sc --> c2 & c3 & c4
c2 & c3 & c4 --> e2
sc --> c5 --> p3 --> e3
p1 -.-> p4
